**Task C1: Replace brand color system with ComfyUI native palette**

Read `ui/web/css/superduper.css` first. Then replace the entire `:root` block with ComfyUI-native colors:

```css
:root {
  /* ComfyUI Native Surfaces */
  --sd-canvas: #1e1e1e;
  --sd-panel: #2b2b2b;
  --sd-card: #353535;
  --sd-card-hover: #3a3a3a;
  --sd-elevated: #404040;
  --sd-input: #1a1a1a;

  /* ComfyUI Native Text */
  --sd-text-primary: #ddd;
  --sd-text-secondary: #aaa;
  --sd-text-muted: #888;
  --sd-text-accent: #ccc;

  /* ComfyUI Native Borders */
  --sd-border: #4e4e4e;
  --sd-border-subtle: #3a3a3a;

  /* Accent (ComfyUI native blue — replaces jade green) */
  --sd-accent: #4e9bcd;
  --sd-accent-dim: #4e9bcd33;
  --sd-accent-subtle: #4e9bcd18;

  /* Keep ALL slot colors unchanged */
  --sd-slot-clip: #FFD500;
  --sd-slot-clip-vision: #A8DADC;
  --sd-slot-conditioning: #FFA931;
  --sd-slot-controlnet: #6EE7B7;
  --sd-slot-image: #64B5F6;
  --sd-slot-latent: #FF9CF9;
  --sd-slot-mask: #81C784;
  --sd-slot-model: #B39DDB;
  --sd-slot-style-model: #C2FFAE;
  --sd-slot-vae: #FF6E6E;
  --sd-slot-noise: #B0B0B0;
  --sd-slot-guider: #66FFFF;
  --sd-slot-sampler: #ECB4B4;
  --sd-slot-sigmas: #CDFFCD;

  /* Typography */
  --sd-font-sans: "Inter", "SF Pro Display", system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
  --sd-font-mono: "JetBrains Mono", "Fira Code", "SF Mono", "Cascadia Code", monospace;

  /* Spacing */
  --sd-space-xs: 4px;
  --sd-space-sm: 6px;
  --sd-space-md: 8px;
  --sd-space-lg: 12px;
  --sd-space-xl: 16px;

  --sd-transition: 150ms ease;
}
```

Then replace ALL occurrences throughout the file:
- `var(--sd-brand)` → `var(--sd-accent)`
- `var(--sd-brand-dim)` → `var(--sd-accent-dim)`
- `var(--sd-brand-subtle)` → `var(--sd-accent-subtle)`
- `var(--sd-text-brand)` → `var(--sd-accent)`
- `var(--sd-dark)` → `#1a1a1a`

Remove the old `--sd-brand`, `--sd-brand-dim`, `--sd-brand-subtle`, `--sd-text-brand`, `--sd-dark` variables entirely (they're replaced in the new :root block above).

**Task C2: Restyle header to match ComfyUI native toolbar**

In `.sd-header`:
- `font-weight: 700` → `font-weight: 500`
- `font-size: 14px` → `font-size: 13px`
- `color: var(--sd-text-brand)` → `color: var(--sd-text-primary)` (after C1 this would be --sd-accent, but we want primary instead)
- `letter-spacing: 0.5px` → `letter-spacing: 0.02em`
- `border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sd-border)` → `border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sd-border-subtle)`

Change `.sd-header__status--connecting` color to `#e6a23c` (warm amber).
Change `.sd-header__status--disconnected` color to `#f56c6c` (ComfyUI error red).

**Task C3: Restyle stage bar**
After the C1 replacements, `.sd-stage-bar` should already use `--sd-accent-subtle`. Just verify `border-bottom` uses `var(--sd-border-subtle)`.

**Task C4: Restyle input bar**
After C1 replacements, `.sd-send-btn` should use `--sd-accent`. Change the text color from `var(--sd-dark)` (which C1 converts to `#1a1a1a`) — verify this is correct. The button text should be dark on the blue accent bg.

Update the file comment at the top to reflect the new design system (no more "Brand: #00BB81").

IMPORTANT: Make ALL changes. Verify there are ZERO remaining references to `sd-brand`, `sd-dark`, or `#00BB81` in the file when you're done.

